@kadinsayani also

https://github.com/canonical/lxd/blob/a2cf2557db3d331151fe9b87de4fa5fd1b27b572/lxd/api_replicators.go#L1179

`Refresh` should always be set to `true` on restore.

@kadinsayani also I am surprised to see that we're creating a snapshot on the B side when doing a restore to the A side:

https://github.com/canonical/lxd/blob/a2cf2557db3d331151fe9b87de4fa5fd1b27b572/lxd/api_replicators.go#L1118-L1130

What was the reason for this? The replicator is only defined on the A side, so was expecting only to create new snapshots on the A side.
